# libpdx-unicode-tables -- utf8 fingerprint golden
#
# Format: one TAG line per expected emission; a `<token>` placeholder
# marks a run-time-filled value that the consumer's klog wrapper
# substitutes in (hex / dec per the brace token's own width).
#
# These are CONTRACT fingerprints, not driver output: this library's
# own primitives are pure leaves that do not emit klog (SRC §"Scope"
# in src/utf8.pdx). A downstream test driver -- or a shell/pds
# consumer that links this library and has a klog capability of its
# own -- is expected to emit these three lines, in this format,
# whenever it invokes the corresponding primitive. The golden tracks
# the format contract so a format drift is caught by `diff` against
# whichever test driver materialises these lines first.
#
# Milestone: M1 (paideia-os#2612, R131.M1).

UTF8 DECODE cp=0x<8-hex> len=<dec>
UTF8 ENCODE cp=0x<8-hex> bytes=<dec>
UTF8 VALID len=<dec> ok=<dec>
